<<<
roast. 1. The use of the p.p. roast is very narrowly limited: roast beef | or hare, but roasted coffee-berries or | cheeks; | Toasted joint; is better roast(ed) than

a roast joint, but a well boiled, but should certainly be roasted. 2. For rule the r., see RULE.
===
**roast.** 1. The use of the p.p. *roast* is very narrowly limited: *roast beef* or *hare*, but *roasted coffee-berries* or *cheeks*; *a roast joint*, but *a well roasted joint*; *is better roast(ed) than boiled*, but *should certainly be roasted*. 2. For *rule the r.*, see ^^RULE^^.
>>>

